# Who owns what. The last matching line wins, so the default comes first.
#
# GitHub asks the owner to review a PR that touches their paths, which is how
# the other person gets pulled in when they edit a module that is not theirs.
# Our own rule is separate and stricter: the OTHER person reviews every PR
# (see CONTRIBUTING.md section 9), so use `gh pr create --reviewer` if GitHub
# did not request them automatically.
#
# Note: automatic review requests from CODEOWNERS may not be available for
# private repositories on a free GitHub plan. The file still documents ownership
# and starts working as soon as the repo is public or the plan allows it.

# Default: both of us
*                                      @nourbouzir @SalmaGz

# Nour: accounts, verification, hosts' offer, discovery, notifications, admin
/app/Modules/Auth/                     @nourbouzir
/app/Modules/Verification/             @nourbouzir
/app/Modules/Experience/               @nourbouzir
/app/Modules/Matching/                 @nourbouzir
/app/Modules/Notification/             @nourbouzir
/app/Modules/Admin/                    @nourbouzir

